ps the"] [145 4 "// strides, so a non-contiguous view stays one)"] [151 42 "// picklebuf_getbuf: the object's own buffer"] [165 4 "// the export of a class's __buffer__: its __release_buffer__ called when the last view goes"] [213 2 "// item and slice assignment into a writable buffer (PY6d's REQUEST: _pyio's readinto, pickle's protocol 5"] [214 2 "// bytearray); byte views only"] [348 4 "// a view of the same memory (writable through a bytearray's)"] [355 20 "// the same memory, so a writable view stays writable (PY6d's REQUEST)"] [368 2 "// count, index and toreadonly (PY7: absent): over tolist's items, as memory_count and memory_index"] [438 3 "// a 1-D view's shape, strides and contiguity (PY7: absent)"] [456 34 "// CHECK_RELEASED (PY7: obj stayed readable; no attribute \"released\", CPython's has none)"] [464 1 "// unusable is the view's CHECK_RELEASED, and its exporter's own check when it has one (queue 204: an mmap closed under"] [465 1 "// the view raises ValueError \"mmap closed or invalid\", where CPython's mmap refuses the close; pyi counts no exports)."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[48 47] [64 55] [77 17] [79 16] [99 17] [99 25] [117 24] [122 24] [122 33] [143 33] [151 35] [152 24] [157 37] [183 25] [190 25] [193 26] [217 25] [237 26] [250 14] [250 21] [296 40] [377 42] [397 42] [408 14] [408 37] [437 80] [470 68]] :go/trails [[452 5]]} (go/file "memoryview.go" :imports [

